From 31c53b78a132c7ca18fd6d6af407aa46fe4c59eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:02:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 418/423] Design check: a shape of hundreds of solids checked
 in seconds, screws in threaded holes

Whether two parts touch (for the floating parts) was distToShape between
the whole shapes: two compounds of hundreds of solids took 100 s a pair,
and a cart of 496 solids ran for more than 23 minutes. Now solid by solid,
only those whose boxes come within the distance, stopping at the first
(a similar model: 222 s to 16 s). The whole-shape distance was also wrong:
nuts on their washers were said to touch nothing. The pin-in-hole test
compares only round faces near each other.

A drawn screw in a threaded hole (a round shank in a hole on the same axis,
smaller by at most a thread's depth, overlapping by no more than that ring)
is told by the shapes and not counted as an overlap; each pair of parts
gets an info line with the number of screws.

--progress shows the design check's steps on stderr; --view given more than
once writes a picture each (no picture was written); the help says the
JSON goes to standard output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
